<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Nadaun</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Nadaun is a town on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/beas">Beas</a> river in the Hamirpur district of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/himachal-pradesh">Himachal Pradesh</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>. Under the Katoch raja Sansar Chand of Kangra in the late 18th and early 19th centuries it was a court residence, and painters working there helped create the Kangra school of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/persian-miniature">miniature painting</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/nadaun.jpg" alt="Nadaun" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Davindermehta · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Mehta.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
